# Working brief, kept locally — deliberately untracked (decisions.md 2026-07-30)
EXTRACTION-BRIEF.md

# The shared core, kept local. `deliverable.md` ("Whose is what") says the build
# machinery is Orin's own IP, reused across clients and never handed over — and
# this remote is public, so tracking it would hand it over. A working adapter
# with its own guardrail and fixtures, not a note about one.
notes/shadcn-adapter/

# The contract templates: MSA and the Diagnostic engagement letter. This remote
# is public, and these carry the legal name, the address line, and the
# commercial terms Orin contracts on. Templates today, filled instruments tomorrow, and the moment a real client
# name or address lands in one there is no undo on a public remote. Untracked
# 2026-08-16; they were tracked before that, so they remain in the history.
notes/contracts/

# Gitdir for the private companion repo (Boyzeeboy/orin-private). Same working
# tree, own index, tracks only the paths excluded above. See scripts/private.
.private.git/

# The Pragma client material. Between them these name Pragma's staff, quote
# what each person said in a real meeting, describe their systems as broken,
# and set out how to sell to them. None of it is untrue and some of it is the
# analysis that won their architect over, but it reads differently to the
# person named than to the person who wrote it. Tracked in orin-private from
# 2026-08-25; they were tracked here before that, so they remain in the history.
notes/pragma-*
scripts/derive-team-proposal.mjs

# The prospect ledger. Same public-remote reasoning as the Pragma block above:
